              "title": "A pedlar's last note",
              "text": "Well, friend, you have come to the bottom of my holes and the end of my thrifty years. My knees tell me the rain before it falls now, and I shan't be coming back down this track to check on my tin.\nKeep the coin, and take the old iron with it: it fed me forty winters and never asked for interest. Put a good ash handle to it and dig your own quiet places.\nFare you well.\nA man who trusts his spade"
